            <ArticleTitle>Differentiation of infectious bronchitis virus vaccine strains Ma5 and 4/91 by TaqMan real-time PCR.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>599-601</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1515/pjvs-2017-0073</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">/j/pjvs.2017.20.issue-3/pjvs-2017-0073/pjvs-2017-0073.xml</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this study was to develop rapid molecular assays for differentiating vaccine strains Ma5 and 4/91 of the infectious bronchitis virus (IBV). Specific primers and probes for S1 and N genes were designed based on the nucleotide sequences of both vaccine strains. Cross-reactivity was not observed. Assay sensitivity was 2.373 × 103 copies of the Ma5 strain, and 3.852 x 103 copies of the 4/91 strain. Samples belonging to a known genotype demonstrated that the designed assays supported rapid and sensitive detection of Ma5 and 4/91 vaccine strains of IBV.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
